    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0120" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24641: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-02T20:00:00+03:00">October 2, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 4—4:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1746. Legation’s 1590, September 7.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d125-f1"/> Letter
                    received today from Smith at Asmara requests that Department be informed that he
                    has returned traveling via the Addis-Asmara Road and resumed charge September
                    27.</p>
                <p>He stated that he is working on report of his trip and requested that following
                    message be sent to Department.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“It is my understanding that the Emperor of Ethiopia has asked President
                        Roosevelt for permission to join the United Nations Pact.<anchor n="23"
                            xml:id="d125-f2"/> What is the status of this request? The admission of
                        Ethiopia is regarded as conditioned upon a declaration of a state of war
                        between Ethiopia and the Axis Powers. Favorable action would facilitate
                        situation for all parties as otherwise Ethiopia is considered neutral.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>In connection with foregoing see my 1033, June 19, 9 p.m.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d125-f3"/> and previous.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
